rew gdu (coreutils).\n  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/du/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n  - No normalization is applied; du output is deterministic when both binaries run on the same directory on the same filesystem.\n  - All block-count tests use -k to pin output to 1024-byte blocks and eliminate platform default divergence.\n  - Tests use a fixture directory (testdata/du-fixture/) containing nested files of known sizes, a second subdirectory for multi-argument tests, and files of varied sizes.\n  - Hard-link pairs are created in test setup (not committed) to test dedup. All files in the fixture are on the same filesystem as the test runner.\n\ntest_cases:\n  - name: du_default_recursive\n    description: Default flags with -k on fixture directory; one line per subdirectory and root.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one \"SIZE\\tPATH\" line per subdirectory, ending with the root directory total\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R1.1\n      - prd009-du R1.2\n      - prd009-du R1.3\n\n  - name: du_summary_mode\n    description: -s prints only the total for each argument.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-sk\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one line with total size and path\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.2\n\n  - name: du_all_files\n    description: -a prints size for every file, not just directories.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-ak\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one line per file and directory in the tree\n      stderr: \"\"\n  